<meta type=article title="Equivalent metadata via kwarg form" author="Ariel Balter">
</meta>

<section | Convergence of kwarg and child-tag <meta> forms>

The two authoring forms of `<meta>` must produce the same Layer 1 child-tag
shape. The `<meta>` above uses the kwarg form; the gate lifts each
allowlisted kwarg to a corresponding child tag. The result is the same as
authoring with explicit `<title>` and `<author>` child tags.

This fixture exercises only the META allowlist keys that have existing
Layer 1 vocabulary entries (title, author, date, subtitle). The other
allowlist entries (doi, license, lang, version, keywords) lift correctly
but their target vocabulary entries are not yet defined — filed as a
finding for a separate vocabulary item, parallel to the missing
<abstract> entry the slice prompt noted.
